    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting to a student’s pace and style. They can offer immediate feedback, explain concepts in different ways, and provide extra practice. This makes learning more engaging and allows students to explore different approaches. It can help teachers focus more on mentoring and less on repetitive drills."
